    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sergeantsville was named after Revolutionary War soldier Charles Sergeant, a local shopkeeper, when the post office opened in 1827.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3,
        4,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergeantsville%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s historic district showcases modest stone and frame homes built from 1773 to 1939, reflecting rural New Jersey architecture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/NJ/Hunterdon_County/Delaware_Township/Sergeantsville_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1886, Sergeantsville Creamery became Hunterdon County’s first creamery, a cooperative that operated until the late 1930s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/NJ/Hunterdon_County/Delaware_Township/Sergeantsville_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every year since 1973, the village hosts “Thanksgiving in the Country,” a house tour that highlights homes with historic, architectural, or cultural significance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergeantsville%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The crossroads that became Sergeantsville first saw a blacksmith, general store, and tavern by the late 1700s, anchoring the village’s early commerce.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
